    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1007">

                <pb facs="0940" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6354/137: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-04T13:00:00+01:00">September 4,
                            1939—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 4—8:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1424. Your 758, September 2, regarding tin; and your 774 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >772</hi>], September 3, 4 p.m., regarding rubber.<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d1007-f1"/> The war has not only closed the Rubber and Tin Exchanges
                    but has created great dislocation in the Government departments concerned with
                    these and other matters. Officials are being transferred to newly created
                    departments such as the Ministry of Economic Warfare and Blockade; in many cases
                    they are unreachable and in any case they are snowed under by a host of problems
                    they have no time to deal with. Further dislocation will be caused when the air
                    bombardments begin. However, I have represented the importance to us of action
                    as regards both rubber and tin and as soon as the position clarifies itself a
                    little I shall do so again. In the meantime I should like to know whether we
                    will have sufficient shipping accommodation so that if necessary we can send our
                    own ships to Malaya to get supplies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
